## EC2 Auto Scaling

### Core Components

#### 1. Launch Template
Defines the configuration for new EC2 instances:
- Amazon Machine Image (AMI)
- Instance type (t3.medium, c5.large, etc.)
- Security groups
- Key pairs
- User data scripts
- Storage configuration
- Monitoring settings

#### 2. Auto Scaling Group (ASG)
Manages a collection of EC2 instances:
- Minimum number of instances
- Maximum number of instances
- Desired capacity
- Availability Zones/Subnets
- Health check configuration
- Scaling policies

#### 3. Scaling Policies
Rules that trigger scaling actions:
- Target Tracking Scaling (recommended)
- Step Scaling
- Scheduled Scaling
- Predictive Scaling

#### 4. Load Balancer Integration
Distributes traffic and provides health checks:
- Application Load Balancer (ALB)
- Network Load Balancer (NLB)
- Classic Load Balancer (CLB)

