## Monitoring & Troubleshooting

### View Scaling Activities

```bash
# Get recent scaling activities
aws autoscaling describe-scaling-activities \
  --auto-scaling-group-name WebAppASG \
  --max-records 10 \
  --query 'Activities[*].[StartTime,EndTime,StatusCode,Description]'

# Monitor in real-time
watch 'aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups \
  --auto-scaling-group-names WebAppASG \
  --query "AutoScalingGroups[0].[DesiredCapacity,Instances[*].InstanceId]"'
```

### CloudWatch Metrics to Monitor

```bash
# CPU Utilization
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/EC2 \
  --metric-name CPUUtilization \
  --start-time 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-01-01T01:00:00Z \
  --period 300 \
  --statistics Average,Maximum

# Target Group Request Count
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/ApplicationELB \
  --metric-name RequestCountPerTarget \
  --start-time 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-01-01T01:00:00Z \
  --period 300 \
  --statistics Sum
```

### Troubleshooting Common Issues

**Issue: Scaling not triggering**
- Check IAM permissions for Auto Scaling service
- Verify CloudWatch metrics are being published
- Check cooldown periods aren't too long
- Ensure target value is realistic

**Issue: Oscillating between scale-up and scale-down**
- Increase cooldown periods
- Adjust target metric value
- Use step scaling for stability

**Issue: Instances not draining properly**
- Enable connection draining on load balancer
- Set lifecycle hooks for graceful shutdown
- Increase termination timeout

